    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **66 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` field so that it returns `true` when the owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching the capacity limit of 50), while leaving the hard rejection at 50 unchanged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added a `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constant and an `isApproachingCityCapacity(city)` method that counts existing owners in the (normalized) city and returns `true` when the count is in `[40, 50)`. Wired it into `addOwner` via `owner.setCapacityWarning(...)`, computed before persistence right alongside the existing `bulkSignupWarning` logic. The hard rejection (`requireCityHasCapacity`, throwing `CityAtCapacityException` at \u226550) already runs earlier and is untouched.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `capacityWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"capacity_warning\")`) with getter/setter, mirroring `bulkSignupWarning`. MapStruct maps it into `OwnerDto` automatically by name.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `capacityWarning` read-only boolean schema property (this generates the `OwnerDto` field).\n\n4. **Schema files** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `capacity_warning` column. The hsqldb profile (used by tests) has `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to be declared explicitly.\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 Its seed inserts use positional (no column list) `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, so I added the corresponding `NULL` to each of the 10 owner rows to keep the value count matching the new column. The other DBs' data.sql files use explicit column lists and needed no change.\n\nThe new `Cp54Tests` (warning) and existing `Cp18Tests` (hard-rejection) both pass, along with the entire suite.",
